{"name":"Calico Cat","hex":"#c48e36","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"calico cat","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tortoiseshell and white domestic cat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calico_cat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calico cat","blocks":[{"text":"A calico cat is a domestic cat of any breed with a tricolor coat of black-based and red-based pigments with white. Outside of North American English, this coat pattern is called tricolor or tortoiseshell and white."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/CalicoCat.jpg/330px-CalicoCat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calico_cat","wikidata":"Q2305997"},{"title":"Calico","blocks":[{"text":"Calico is a heavy plain-woven textile made from unbleached, and often not fully processed, cotton. It may also contain unseparated husk parts. The fabric is coarser than muslin, but less coarse and thick than canvas or denim. It is still very cheap owing to its unfinished and undyed appearance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Calico_Sample.JPG/330px-Calico_Sample.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calico","wikidata":"Q1132695"},{"title":"Cat","blocks":[{"text":"The cat, also called domestic cat and house cat, is a small domesticated carnivorous mammal. It is a member of Felidae, the family of mammals in the order Carnivora also colloquially referred to as cats. An obligate carnivore requiring a predominantly meat-based diet, it has retractable claws adapted to killing small prey species such as mice and rats. It has a strong, flexible body, quick reflexes, and sharp teeth, and its night vision and sense of smell are well developed. It is a social species, but a solitary hunter and a crepuscular predator.\nCat communication includes meowing, purring, trilling, hissing, growling, grunting, body language, and scent marking. It can hear sounds too faint or too high in frequency for human ears, such as those made by small mammals. It secretes and perceives pheromones. Cat intelligence is evident in its ability to adapt, learn through observation, and solve problems. The domestic cat is the only domesticated species of the family Felidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Siam_lilacpoint.jpg/330px-Siam_lilacpoint.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat","wikidata":"Q146"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Calico_cat.png/500px-Calico_cat.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Calico_cat.png/1280px-Calico_cat.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Calico_cat.png/500px-Calico_cat.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalico_cat.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/British_Shorthair_tricolore.jpg/500px-British_Shorthair_tricolore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/British_Shorthair_tricolore.jpg/500px-British_Shorthair_tricolore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABritish_Shorthair_tricolore.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Taiwanese_Dominantly_Black_Calico_Cat.jpg/500px-Taiwanese_Dominantly_Black_Calico_Cat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c